# Normalize line endings across platforms.
#
# Why this matters: on Windows, git's default `core.autocrlf` may convert
# LF -> CRLF on checkout. Without this file, contributors on Windows and
# contributors on macOS/Linux would see different bytes on disk for the
# same file, breaking tooling that's strict about line endings (golangci-
# lint, shfmt, etc.) and producing noisy diffs.
#
# `text=auto` tells git to normalize line endings to LF in the repo, and
# convert based on platform on checkout. The explicit lines below ensure
# LF on disk for files that always need LF (shell scripts, Go source, etc).

* text=auto

# Files that must be LF regardless of platform.
*.go        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
justfile    text eol=lf

# Binary files (no normalization).
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
